# Critical distinction: `resolve("D")`

This:

```js
resolve("D");
```

means:

> Fulfill the Promise with the value `"D"`.

It does **not** mean:

```js
console.log("D");
```

Instead, `"D"` becomes the value received by:

```js
.then(value => {
    console.log("E", value);
});
```

So:

```text
E D
```

is printed.

